  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Inclusive Education II 2017-2019 - UNICEF Basic Education</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNICEF Inclusive Education II 2017-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of UNICEF&#x2019;s Inclusive Education programme 2017-2019 is to support Cambodia in providing and assuring more equitable provision of quality education services. This is expected to be achieved by fulfilling four outcomes, which include support for research, data and coordination, tailored programmes to increase boys&#x2019; and girls&#x2019; participation in education with a component on climate change adaptation, strategies to strengthen the quality of the teaching and learning process including learning assessments, life skills and the implementation of the external and internal inspection framework.  1. By 2019, there is strengthened capacity for policy development and coordination in education. 2. By 2019, there is increased capacity and accountability to provide access to inclusive basic education particularly amongst indigenous minorities and children with disabilities including in emergencies. 3. By 2019, there is strengthened capacity of education authorities at national level and in targeted districts to provide quality and measurable primary and lower secondary education. 4. There is sustained UNICEF technical support to the education sector with a focus on the most marginalised children.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programmet bygger p&#xe5; tidigare UNICEF program inom utbildningssektorn i Kambodja riktade mot barn och ungdomar (PlanIT 51100073, UNICEF - Inclusive Education Support 2014-2016, 30 MSEK). Programmet har ett tydligare fokus p&#xe5; l&#xe4;rande &#xe4;n f&#xf6;reg&#xe5;ende fas, inklusive kunskapsutv&#xe4;rdering och genomf&#xf6;rande av det kvalitetsutv&#xe4;rderingssystem som initierades i samarbete med svenska Skolinspektionen (PlanIT 51100054 Education Quality Assurance 2013-2016, 16,5 MSEK). Programmet har fortsatt tyngdpunkt p&#xe5; insatser f&#xf6;r barn fr&#xe5;n etniska minoritetsgrupper, barn som lever med funktionsneds&#xe4;ttningar och andra utsatta grupper. J&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet i olika former, inklusive insatser f&#xf6;r att motverka skolrelaterad k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld, samt WASH (vatten, sanitet och hygien) har en mer framtr&#xe4;dande roll i denna programfas j&#xe4;mf&#xf6;rt med tidigare. Ett nytt inslag i programmet &#xe4;r arbetet med klimat och milj&#xf6;fr&#xe5;gor. Sammantaget har d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r det nya tre&#xe5;rsst&#xf6;det en &#xf6;kad total avtalsvolym (57 MSEK) j&#xe4;mf&#xf6;rt med tidigare fas (30 MSEK).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed programme is to a certain extend a continuation of the Sweden funded programme  - UNICEF - Inclusive Education Support 2014-2016 (51100073). The proposed new phase will have stronger focus on children&#x2019;s learning, including learning assessments and the operationalisation of the quality assurance system that was initiated in twinning cooperation with the Swedish School Inspectorate.  The programme will maintain important equity interventions for children from ethnic minorities, children with disabilities and over-aged children. This phase of the proposed programme will have clearer focus on gender issues &#x2013; including school related gender based violence and WASH. A new part of the programme is a emphasis on climate change and environmental issues.</narrative>
  </description>
